p anchor exists recheck before TERM/KILL; do not infer ownership merely from port/name. Reap/remove only recorded own inode-safe temp root after group absent; reserved manifests with no helper/serve may clean only their proven owned root. No name-wide kill or scanning outside registry.\",\n           \"directory_cleanup\": \"Parent-alive cleanup verifies helper+serve/group gone before rmtree; parent-dead helper uses terminal_quiescence (all residual writers stopped, helper owns PGID, root/inode/UID verified) before final self-including KILL. This narrowly defined terminal path is the only cleanup-before-group-absence path; no deletion while unquiesced child can recreate files. Only recorded zen-serve-state-* local root resolved under tempfile.gettempdir, correct uid+inode/no symlink. Foreign roots never removed; no ignore_errors; failed cleanup retains manifest for startup reaper.\",\n@@ -2172,3 +2523,4 @@\n             \"VER-005\"\n-          ]\n+          ],\n+          \"helper_cli_contract\": \"Helper argv=[sys.executable, \\\"-I\\\", str(Path(__file__).resolve()), \\\"--serve-helper\\\", attempt_id, str(port), ...]; start_new_session=True, child_pgid=helper_proc.pid. CLI dispatcher is inside if __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\": after existing import zen_catalog as zc and before main()/HTTP startup; all typed _run_serve_helper_cli(...) code resides directly in server.py, checked by Ruff/basedpyright with zero new Any/E402. No inline -c source, no new helper module. --serve-helper <attempt_id> follows script path at the front of ps argv, before port/other parameters; reaper verifies exact script realpath, argv position, full untruncated ps -ww command, attempt_id, UID/PID/lstart/PGID and manifest. Never put password or prompt in argv.\"\n         }\n@@ -2280,3 +2632,4 @@\n           \"env_prefix\": \"OPENCODE_ZEN_BRIDGE_\",\n-          \"validation\": \"положительное finite число; недопустимое -> ошибка старта, не бесконечный timeout\"\n+          \"validation\": \"п